// The parser bounds how deeply a pattern may nest, as it bounds an
// expression, and says so once.
//
// Every pass after the parser walks a pattern one level at a time, so the
// bound is what lets a deep pattern be reported rather than exhaust a stack.
// Each enum below carries the one before it, so a pattern for `Level1000`
// may name a variant at every level. The pattern written here does, and its
// innermost levels stand past the limit.
